{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cesi6D4JLTjhLPbGbkVTP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The cancel order feature is fully implemented and tested. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n**Files Modified:**\n1. **Order.kt** - Added `OrderStatus` enum (`ACTIVE`, `CANCELLED`) and a `status` field to the Order data class\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Added `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint with complete cancel logic\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added `findByOrderId()` method to find all shipments for an order\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added validation to prevent creating shipments for cancelled orders\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Added error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT`\n\n**Key Features Implemented:**\n- ✅ Orders start in `ACTIVE` status, transition to `CANCELLED` when cancelled\n- ✅ `GET /orders/{orderId}` reports the order status\n- ✅ `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an order and all its `CREATED` shipments\n- ✅ Idempotent cancellation - cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds with no changes\n- ✅ All-or-nothing validation - if any shipment is `CONFIRMED`, the cancel is rejected with 409 and nothing changes\n- ✅ Non-existent orders return 404\n- ✅ Creating shipments for cancelled orders is rejected with 409\n- ✅ Error responses follow the existing API error envelope pattern\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- All 4 existing order tests pass\n- All 5 existing shipment tests pass\n- 8 new tests for cancel functionality covering all scenarios\n- Total: 21 tests, 0 failures\n\nNo new Maven dependencies were added, and only the order, shipment, and shared API packages were modified as required."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":427,"cache_read_input_tokens":52352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ep